# Files that live in the repository but must NOT ship inside the scaffold ZIP.
# `scripts/build-scaffold-release.sh` builds the release with `git archive`,
# which honours `export-ignore`.
#
# .github/ is repository infrastructure for myICOR/myPKA itself, not scaffold
# content, and it is already outside the declared contract: it appears in
# neither manifest.json `framework_paths` nor `user_state_paths`, so the
# updater has never managed it. Shipping it also pushed myICOR's own Supabase
# project URL, edge-function name and CI secret NAMES into every member's
# folder, and handed anyone building a derivative a release pipeline aimed at
# our infrastructure rather than theirs. Issue and PR templates point at our
# tracker and are equally useless in a member's vault.
.github/ export-ignore
.gitattributes export-ignore
.privacy-guard.json export-ignore
